# Exported viewer traces: regenerable from scripts/export_trace.py, and they
# multiply with every controller, seed and profile, so the default is to ignore
# them and keep named exceptions.
#
# Four are committed. Three are a constant-flow sweep over one held-out profile
# (actions 0.1, 0.4 and 1.0), which is what the viewer's first two beats need:
# comparing heat against the cost of cooling requires more than one flow level,
# and 0.1 is the one that breaks the limit. The fourth is the loader fixture at
# action 0.3 on another profile. Add a line here to keep another.
results/traces/*.json
!results/traces/manifest.json
!results/traces/constant_action0.1_partial_seed0_test00.json
!results/traces/constant_action0.3_partial_seed0_test07.json
!results/traces/constant_action0.4_partial_seed0_test00.json
!results/traces/constant_action1_partial_seed0_test00.json
